{
  "_comment": "A tilemap demo. The level is ONE entity with a TilemapComponent: the grid holds a small number per cell, and what each number looks like lives in a .otile file. Nothing here says which of the 47 shapes a cell is - that is worked out from its neighbours every frame. See engine/include/engine/tilemap/AutoTile.h.",
  "_connectors": "The bottom row, at y = -1, is CONNECTOR tiles: invisible, but the stone above believes the ground carries on through them, so the floor runs off the bottom of the screen instead of growing a finished edge. They show as faint magenta in the Scene view only.",
  "_try": "Open the Tile Palette panel, choose a tile and a brush, and paint. The walls become solid as you draw them, because TilemapColliderComponent watches the map and merges the solid cells into boxes.",
